**New evidence**
I added six new source-claim units from the 2022 budget speech, Hasina’s Smart Bangladesh speech, and crisis-response reporting.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Hasina unveils plan to transition to 'Smart Bangladesh' by 2041","publisher":"bdnews24.com","publication_date":"2022-12-12","url":"https://bdnews24.com/bangladesh/6fv5wmbti6","claim":"Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina revealed the government's Smart Bangladesh program, saying the country would move from digital to smart Bangladesh by 2041 and that the plan rested on four pillars: smart citizens, smart economy, smart government, and smart society.","locator":"article lead / opening summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report of a direct PM announcement; secondary but specific and attributable.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year, December 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High: the program is explicitly framed as Hasina's national direction; the article reports her own announcement rather than a later interpretation.","contrary_evidence":["This is a plan announcement, not proof that the 2041 goals were achieved in 2022.","Later macro pressures show the vision coexisted with significant economic constraints."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National Budget Speech 2022-2023","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Bangladesh","publication_date":"2022-06-09","url":"https://bangladeshcustoms.gov.bd/budget/National_Budget_Speech_FY2022-23_English_Version.pdf","claim":"The budget speech says the social safety net was being expanded to reduce poverty and inequality, that 29 percent of households were covered, and that FY2022-23 social safety-net allocation was Tk 113,576 crore (2.55 percent of GDP), with the NSSS Action Plan 2021-26 underway.","locator":"pp. 95-97; lines 2497-2526 and 2656-2658","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget speech with specific, time-bound program and spending claims, though still self-reporting by the government.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 budget cycle and the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High: this is a core executive budget instrument under Hasina's government, though authored by the finance ministry rather than the PM personally.","contrary_evidence":["The claim is government self-report and needs independent execution data to confirm delivery at scale.","Allocation and coverage do not alone prove quality or targeting accuracy."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National Budget Speech 2022-2023","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Bangladesh","publication_date":"2022-06-09","url":"https://bangladeshcustoms.gov.bd/budget/National_Budget_Speech_FY2022-23_English_Version.pdf","claim":"The budget speech says e-governance had digitalized about 2,000 public services, 8,363 digital centres were operating nationwide, 1.66 crore files had been handled through e-filing, and the e-GP system had improved procurement transparency by March 2022.","locator":"pp. 103-105; lines 2728-2746","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget document with concrete implementation claims and operational figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and tied to implementation by March 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High: these are direct state-execution claims under the Hasina-led government, though some details may overstate quality or user experience.","contrary_evidence":["The speech reports outputs, not independent verification of service quality or equity.","Digitization counts can overstate real-world reach if service quality lags behind rollout."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.5","8B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National Budget Speech 2022-2023","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Bangladesh","publication_date":"2022-06-09","url":"https://bangladeshcustoms.gov.bd/budget/National_Budget_Speech_FY2022-23_English_Version.pdf","claim":"The budget speech says the government was prioritizing Fourth Industrial Revolution readiness by expanding technical education and ICT training, with targets to train more than 60,000 young people by 2025 and 100,000 by 2030, while 2.34 lakh people had already been trained through BCC programs.","locator":"pp. 102-103; lines 2680-2707","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget speech with concrete training targets and reported training outputs.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the 2022 budget cycle.","ruler_attribution":"High: this is a government training and curriculum agenda under Hasina's administration, though the finance ministry delivered the speech.","contrary_evidence":["Training targets do not prove labor-market absorption or productivity gains.","The figures are program outputs, not audited evidence of long-term effectiveness."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6"]}

